From 8d0387da9f90a7fc9948795fca4841f188702ea3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 21:33:01 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] v3.0.0: open the release rung

The v3.0.0 milestone. Carries the v2.9.6-v2.9.9a work already in canon:
the four upstream 3006.102.9 pull-forwards (tor 0.4.9.11, its IPv6
anti-leak, the Brahma-B53 mitigation whitelist, the OpenSSL 1.1.1 CMS+DTLS
CVE backports), the native Backup & Restore redesign with the landing-page
Complete-restore banner, the full translation + spelling review across all
25 dictionaries, and the v3.0.0-gate security remediation (DNS Traffic
Analyzer SQLi, the restore-parser overflow guard, the sdn_rl template
breakout, and CSV formula injection).

Ships on OpenSSL 1.1.1w with the CVE backports (the 3.5 migration is
deferred pending the GPL-licence decision); manifest signing stays inert.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 release/src-rt/version.conf | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/release/src-rt/version.conf b/release/src-rt/version.conf
index 0dae0f81ba..83275b04c8 100644
--- a/release/src-rt/version.conf
+++ b/release/src-rt/version.conf
@@ -4,6 +4,6 @@ KERNEL_VER_AM=$(subst .,,$(KERNEL_VER))
 FS_VER_AM=$(subst .,,$(FS_VER))
 
 SERIALNO=102.8
-EXTENDNO=Reaper_v2.9.9a
+EXTENDNO=Reaper_v3.0.0
 
 RCNO=0
-- 
2.25.1

